arbeitnow:senior-front-end-engineer-reac:
&lt;h2&gt;In a nutshell&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Picnic, we're revolutionising the way people buy groceries with our affordable and sustainable grocery service. In the Personalization team, you’ll build the experimentation platform that lets Picnic try new ideas safely and at scale: from which promotions to highlight to which emails to send. Your work lets business teams run experiments and control the customer experience themselves, without needing an engineer for every change. It’s a product that is foundational to our business, and it directly improves how customers shop every day. &lt;br&gt;We use React, React Native and TypeScript across the board, together with&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://blog.picnic.nl/faster-features-happier-customers-introducing-the-platform-that-transformed-our-grocery-app-b38e57a85531" target="_blank"&gt;our server-driven UI framework&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; and we’re working towards a single platform for mobile and web.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Tricks of the trade&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Think like a product owner.&lt;/strong&gt; You don’t just implement requirements, you question them. Together with product owners and designers, you shape specifications for new features, discuss trade-offs, push back when something doesn’t add up, and help build a long-term vision for where the platform should go.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build bridges.&lt;/strong&gt; You work with cross-functional teams across the whole business: the business teams who rely on the platform, fellow engineers, and the other consumer-facing teams whose features run through it. You make it easy for others to succeed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive things forward.&lt;/strong&gt; You don’t wait for someone to hand you the next task. You spot what could be better, in the codebase, the platform or how the team works, and you take the lead on fixing it. You’ll take on increasingly challenging projects with full ownership of your contributions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Tech:&lt;/strong&gt; React, React Native, TypeScript and RxJS, Redux, Styled Components, Jest, Storybook&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you want ownership, real influence on product direction, and to see your work reach millions of customers, you’ll feel at home here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;We’re looking for&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of building and shipping frontend applications end-to-end. You’ve taken products from idea to millions of users, and you’ve stayed around to make them better.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong conceptual thinker. You thrive in ambiguity and lead the way to the right solution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sharp judgement on trade-offs. You know when to build it right and when to ship it now, and you make that call yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real curiosity about the customer. You care whether your work changes how people shop, not just whether the code is clean.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, structured communicator. You collaborate effectively with product, design, backend, analytics, and frontend teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine motivation to build consumer and e-commerce experiences used by millions, with willingness to work from&lt;strong class="text-green1 list-item-text"&gt;&amp;nbsp;Picnic’s Amsterdam office-first environment&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Picnic Perks&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;✍🏼Every expert was once a beginner!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll get plenty of opportunities to challenge yourself and grow, including the Picnic Tech Academy, Lunch &amp;amp; Learn sessions, and tailored soft skills training. We also offer free professional weekly language courses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💡Make a difference&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work in an awesome startup environment with the freedom to drive your own projects and create a visible impact. Our fully electric vehicles and sustainable business model mean you’ll also be contributing to making the world a better place!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🫱🏼‍🫲🏾Teamwork makes the dream work&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With more than 80 nationalities across 3 countries, you’ll be part of a diverse company with plenty of cool stuff to get involved with, from board game evenings to after-work drinks to our company ski trip and more!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🍎You are what you eat&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll get freshly prepared, healthy lunches and snacks (with plenty of vegetarian, vegan, and halal options). Coffee snob? Don’t worry, our amazing Picnic barista has you covered.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🚴🏽Stay healthy&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mental health is important. As well as having the option to speak with Picnic colleagues who act as confidential advisors, our collaboration with OpenUp gives you easy access to professional psychologists, along with workshops and materials.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There are plenty of sports communities and events to get involved with, from tennis to yoga, to climbing!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🔋Attractive package&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We offer competitive compensation and a pension plan that looks out for your future self, as well as 25 vacation days per year, so you can recharge your batteries&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌍Benefits for expats&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It can be daunting starting a new job AND moving to a new country. That’s why we offer lots of support for our many expat colleagues, if you want to find our relocation benefits, see&lt;a href="https://jobs.picnic.app/en/relocation"&gt; here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</p>

arbeitnow:golang-backend-engineer-financ:
&lt;div class="content-intro"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Global Structure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Deliveroo is now part of DoorDash, bringing together teams with even greater reach, scale, and ambition. Depending on your role, you may collaborate with teammates, systems, and leaders across DoorDash and Wolt. Together, we’re unlocking new possibilities as one global team.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Your job is to make sure every payout and transaction lands with the right person.&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have spent years getting very good at protecting the things a marketplace has always had to protect: checkout fraud, account takeover, courier abuse. But we are no longer only a marketplace. We now issue banking products, lend to merchants, move instant payouts to couriers, and collect cash on the doorstep. Every one of those is a new way for money to leave the platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a new team, and it owns that surface: fraud wherever money moves through the platform. Who receives it, who lends it, who collects it, and who holds it in a financial account. Think instant payout rails, merchant cash advances, and platform-issued banking and earned-wage products serving millions of couriers and merchants. These are live loss surfaces, and the volume grows with every financial product we launch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are now looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Backend Engineer (Golang)&lt;/strong&gt; to build that protection. You will design and ship real-time detection and automated enforcement for our financial products across DoorDash, Wolt, and Deliveroo. The work is high-throughput, low-latency, and unusually consequential: a rule you ship on Monday can stop a serious loss by Friday. It is also close to greenfield, so you will be setting the patterns every future financial product inherits on day one.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will be based in &lt;strong&gt;London&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;UK&lt;/strong&gt; as one of the founding engineering roles in our London hub, working closely with our teams in Helsinki and Berlin.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you'll do:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain high-throughput, low-latency backend services in Go that score financial events in real time, including payout enrollments, bank account links, credit applications, and account-to-account transfers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design fraud detection and automated enforcement for our financial products end to end: from signal collection through to the decision that blocks a fraudulent payout.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build on and extend our shared fraud decisioning platform, so signals, rules, and models work across all three of our brands instead of being rebuilt three times.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with risk analysts, data scientists, and product managers to turn observed fraud patterns into shipped detection, and to know when a rule, a model, or a product change is the right answer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across team boundaries with our account security, payments fraud, and financial product teams. We build on their signals rather than rebuild them, so clean interfaces matter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to architectural discussions and technical decisions as we establish the fraud infrastructure baseline for financial products, with support from senior engineers on the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write well-tested, observable code and help the team hold a high quality bar. In fraud, a silent failure is a loss event.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Our expectations:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3 to 6 years of professional software engineering experience, including backend services you have shipped and owned in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of production experience in Golang, or strong experience in another backend language and real enthusiasm for picking Go up quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A working understanding of low-latency, high-throughput distributed systems. Real-time decisioning comes with a latency budget, and you are keen to learn to build inside one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with SQL and/or NoSQL databases, and some exposure to event-driven architectures (Kafka or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to operate what you build, including a share of on-call, with a pragmatic approach to reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uses AI tooling in day-to-day development and can critically evaluate its output for correctness and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in fraud, risk, payments, lending, or financial crime, especially money movement fraud, bank account linking fraud, payout abuse, or lending fraud.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with rules engines, real-time feature stores, or ML model serving in a decisioning path.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in Kotlin, Java, Python, or Node.js alongside Go.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with cloud infrastructure (AWS, GCP).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across multiple brands, regions, or regulatory regimes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we value&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A product-oriented mindset. You think beyond the ticket, understand the "why" behind the work, and take a high level of responsibility for outcomes rather than output.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with ambiguity. This is a new team on a new surface; parts of the charter are still being drawn, and you will help draw them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of owning a project or feature end to end, especially in fast-paced environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear and proactive communication, with a collaborative spirit. We work across three companies and several time zones, so we move fast, but we succeed together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An adversarial instinct. The best fraud engineers enjoy thinking like the attacker.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class="content-conclusion"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diversity, Equity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;At Deliveroo, we know that a great workplace reflects the world around us and that true diversity and inclusion make us stronger, more creative, and better at what we do. We’re committed to fostering an environment where everyone can do their best work and feel they belong.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in equality of opportunity and welcome candidates from all backgrounds regardless of age, gender, ethnicity, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, socio-economic background, religion, or belief.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you have a disability or long-term health condition and need support to apply for one of our roles, or require any reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process, you’ll have the opportunity to let us know once you’ve submitted your application. We’ll share details on how to request support so we can ensure you have a fair and equitable experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re excited about making a real impact in a fast-moving marketplace and growing your career alongside ambitious, supportive teams, we’d love to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-renderer-mark="true"&gt;&lt;br&gt;Beware of recruitment scams: DASH Brands will never ask you to pay money or share sensitive financial information during hiring — learn more about DASH Brands' legitimate recruiting process at&lt;/em&gt; &lt;a class="_ymio1r31 _ypr0glyw _zcxs1o36 _mizu194a _1ah3dkaa _ra3xnqa1 _128mdkaa _1cvmnqa1 _4davt94y _4bfu18uv _1hms8stv _ajmmnqa1 _vchhusvi _kqswh2mm _2rkolb4i _ect4ttxp _syaz13af _1a3b18uv _4fpr8stv _5goinqa1 _f8pj13af _9oik18uv _1bnxglyw _jf4cnqa1 _30l313af _1nrm18uv _c2waglyw _1iohnqa1 _9h8h12zz _10531ra0 _1ien1ra0 _n0fx1ra0 _1vhv17z1" href="http://careersatdoordash.com/recruitment-scam-awareness" data-renderer-mark="true" data-is-router-link="false" data-testid="link-with-safety"&gt;&lt;em data-renderer-mark="true"&gt;careersatdoordash.com/recruitment-scam-awareness&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em data-renderer-mark="true"&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</p>

arbeitnow:senior-infrastructure-engineer:
&lt;h2&gt;About Nscale&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nscale is the GPU cloud engineered for AI. We provide cost-effective, high-performance infrastructure for AI start-ups and large enterprise customers. Nscale enables AI-focused companies to achieve superior results by reducing the complexity of AI development. Our GPU cloud bolsters technical capabilities and directly supports strategic business outcomes, including cost management, rapid innovation, and environmental responsibility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We thrive on a culture of relentless innovation, ownership, and accountability, where every team member takes pride in their work and drives it with excellence and urgency. As an Nscaler, you’ll build trust through openness and transparency, where everyone is inspired to do their best work. If you join our team, you’ll be contributing to building the technology that powers the future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re hiring an &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Infrastructure Engineer (OpenStack Ironic Specialist)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; to design, operate, and continuously improve the bare metal provisioning platforms that underpin Nscale’s infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits within the &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Infrastructure Engineering team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, which is responsible for the design, implementation, operation, and ongoing improvement of the infrastructure stack supporting both internal and customer-facing services. You’ll work closely with &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;network, compute, data centre, support, and pre-sales teams&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, while also serving as a specialist escalation point for advanced provisioning and hardware issues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-impact role focused on &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;OpenStack Ironic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, automated hardware lifecycle management, and the reliable operation of large-scale physical infrastructure. You’ll also help connect Nscale to the broader &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;upstream OpenStack community&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, ensuring our bare metal platforms evolve in line with real operational needs and industry direction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you'll be doing&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Bare Metal Provisioning &amp;amp; Lifecycle Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value="1"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Design&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; scalable and resilient bare metal provisioning platforms with a strong focus on &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;OpenStack Ironic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value="2"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Own&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; the full lifecycle of physical infrastructure, including discovery, enrolment, provisioning, cleaning, deprovisioning, and hardware state management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value="3"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Build&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; and maintain provisioning workflows for a wide range of hardware profiles, including &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;GPU-enabled&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; and high-performance server platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value="4"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; platform upgrades, lifecycle management, and operational improvements across &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Ironic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; and its dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Automation &amp;amp; Platform Integration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value="1"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Manage&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; and improve integrations between &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Ironic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; and related OpenStack services such as &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Nova, Neutron, Glance, Keystone, and Placement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value="2"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Drive&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; automation for hardware onboarding, firmware and BIOS configuration, deployment workflows, validation, and recovery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value="3"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Implement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; infrastructure automation using &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;infrastructure-as-code&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; and configuration management approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value="4"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Ensure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; provisioning platforms and operational processes align with security, compliance, and operational standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Troubleshooting, Reliability &amp;amp; Operational Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value="1"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Troubleshoot&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; complex issues across provisioning pipelines, &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;PXE/iPXE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, BMC interfaces, out-of-band management, image deployment, network boot, and hardware compatibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value="2"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Act&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; as a &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;3rd/4th line escalation point&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; for advanced bare metal and provisioning incidents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value="3"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Perform&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; root cause analysis and implement long-term fixes to improve platform reliability and repeatability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value="4"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Participate&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; in on-call rotations and incident response activities for critical infrastructure services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration &amp;amp; Community Engagement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value="1"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Collaborate&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; with network, compute, data centre, and support teams to deliver reliable physical infrastructure services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value="2"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Contribute&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; specialist input to infrastructure roadmap planning, capacity expansion, standard builds, and hardware platform qualification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value="3"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; pre-sales and solution design efforts with expert guidance on bare metal capabilities, operational models, and deployment constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value="4"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Contribute&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; to upstream OpenStack bare metal communities through bug reports, testing, reviews, design discussions, and code contributions where appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value="5"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Track&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; upstream roadmaps and release changes to help shape Nscale’s bare metal strategy, upgrade planning, and platform standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;KPIs&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value="1"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Automated provisioning and hardware onboarding reliability&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value="2"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Bare metal incident resolution and root cause closure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value="3"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Platform upgrade and lifecycle delivery across Ironic dependencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value="4"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Upstream OpenStack Ironic community contribution and adoption alignment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About You&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value="1"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Strong experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; operating Linux systems and troubleshooting production infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value="2"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Strong specialist knowledge&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; of &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;OpenStack Ironic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; and the surrounding provisioning ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value="3"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Strong understanding&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; of bare metal provisioning concepts including &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;PXE/iPXE, DHCP, TFTP/HTTP boot, BMC technologies, RAID configuration, firmware management, disk imaging, and node lifecycle states&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value="4"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Strong experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; with out-of-band management technologies such as &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Redfish, IPMI, or vendor management interfaces&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value="5"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Strong experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; designing and building automation for physical and virtual infrastructure using tools such as &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Ansible&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value="6"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Strong scripting skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; in &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Python and Bash&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value="7"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; troubleshooting complex provisioning and hardware integration issues across server, network, and management layers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value="8"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; operating infrastructure at scale with a focus on reliability, repeatability, and operational safety&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value="9"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Ability&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; to collaborate across infrastructure, support, and architecture teams to solve complex technical problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value="10"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; contributing to or working closely with upstream open-source communities, particularly &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class="textBold"&gt;OpenStack, Ironic, Metal3, or related infrastructure projects&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, is highly desirable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we can offer you&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Nscale, you'll find a collaborative, supportive, and innovative environment where your contributions spark real impact. We're building something extraordinary, and we want you at the core.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Highly competitive US compensation package (base + bonus + equity), with performance reviews every 12 months. 🚀&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join one of the fastest-growing AI infrastructure companies — your chance to directly shape how global AI capacity is planned and deployed. ✨&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Expect a dynamic progression plan tailored to your ambitions. Grow by leading critical cross-functional initiatives and shaping capital strategy — always with our full support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Human-First Flexibility: We treat you as humans first. 🫶🏽 Our flexible workplace trusts Nscalers to deliver, giving you the autonomy to shape your day around life's moments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Equal Opportunities Statement&lt;/h2&gt;
